{
  "_readme": [
    "Semantic vocabularies for canonical fields whose VALUE is unambiguous but whose",
    "MEANING is not. Three of the 23 fields have this shape:",
    "",
    "  Date      a date, but which date? transaction / registration / handover / lease",
    "  Size      a number, but in what unit? sq ft / sq m",
    "  AREA      a place, but at what level? Community / Sub-Community",
    "",
    "These are data, not code. Adding a date_type is an edit to this file plus an",
    "ENGINE_VERSION bump -- never a code change. Order within 'types' is the tie-break",
    "order used when two types score equally, so put the most common first.",
    "",
    "Signals, strongest first. A reading made from fewer signals scores lower,",
    "which is what routes it to review rather than into a confident wrong answer.",
    "",
    "signals.header      substrings matched against the ORIGINAL source header",
    "signals.value       substrings matched against sample VALUES -- the source",
    "                    stating its own unit ('1,250 sq.m') outranks any header",
    "signals.neighbour   canonical fields mapped elsewhere on the same sheet",
    "signals.companion   other raw headers on the same sheet",
    "signals.sheet       substrings matched against the worksheet name",
    "signals.workbook    substrings matched against the source filename",
    "signals.vocabulary  known values; matched against the column's own values",
    "min_confidence      below this the observation is routed to review, never guessed"
  ],
